Lab 20: Virtual Machine Migration Between Clusters
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

• Set up and configure a multi-cluster OpenShift environment for VM migration • Understand the concepts and requirements for cross-cluster VM migration • Use virtctl and OpenShift tools to migrate virtual machines between clusters • Verify VM functionality and data integrity after migration • Troubleshoot common migration issues and implement best practices • Implement proper networking and storage considerations for cross-cluster migrations

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

• Basic understanding of OpenShift Container Platform concepts • Familiarity with Kubernetes resources (pods, services, persistent volumes) • Experience with OpenShift Virtualization (CNV) fundamentals • Knowledge of Linux command line operations • Understanding of virtualization concepts and VM lifecycle management • Basic networking knowledge (VLANs, subnets, routing)

Required Tools
• Access to two OpenShift clusters with OpenShift Virtualization installed • virtctl CLI tool • oc CLI tool • kubectl CLI tool • SSH access to cluster nodes (if needed)

Ready-to-Use Cloud Machines
Al Nafi provides pre-configured Linux-based cloud machines for this lab. Simply click Start Lab to access your environment. No need to build your own VMs or configure the initial setup - everything is ready for you to begin the migration exercises immediately.

