Task 1: Set Up Multi-Cluster OpenShift Environment
Subtask 1.1: Verify Cluster Access and Configuration
First, let's verify access to both OpenShift clusters and ensure they're properly configured for VM migration.

Step 1: Check Source Cluster Access

# Set context for source cluster
export SOURCE_CLUSTER_URL="https://api.source-cluster.example.com:6443"
export SOURCE_CLUSTER_TOKEN="your-source-cluster-token"

# Login to source cluster
oc login --token=$SOURCE_CLUSTER_TOKEN --server=$SOURCE_CLUSTER_URL

# Verify cluster status
oc get nodes
oc get clusterversion
Step 2: Check Destination Cluster Access

# Set context for destination cluster
export DEST_CLUSTER_URL="https://api.dest-cluster.example.com:6443"
export DEST_CLUSTER_TOKEN="your-dest-cluster-token"

# Login to destination cluster
oc login --token=$DEST_CLUSTER_TOKEN --server=$DEST_CLUSTER_URL

# Verify cluster status
oc get nodes
oc get clusterversion
Step 3: Verify OpenShift Virtualization Installation

# Check on source cluster
oc login --token=$SOURCE_CLUSTER_TOKEN --server=$SOURCE_CLUSTER_URL
oc get csv -n openshift-cnv | grep kubevirt

# Check on destination cluster
oc login --token=$DEST_CLUSTER_TOKEN --server=$DEST_CLUSTER_URL
oc get csv -n openshift-cnv | grep kubevirt
Subtask 1.2: Configure Network Connectivity Between Clusters
Step 1: Verify Network Connectivity

# From source cluster, test connectivity to destination
oc get nodes -o wide

# Note the external IPs and test connectivity
ping <destination-cluster-node-ip>
Step 2: Configure DNS Resolution (if needed)

# Add DNS entries for cross-cluster communication
# This may require cluster administrator privileges

cat << EOF > /tmp/cluster-dns-config.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: cluster-dns-config
  namespace: openshift-config
data:
  Corefile: |
    .:53 {
        errors
        health
        ready
        kubernetes cluster.local in-addr.arpa ip6.arpa {
            pods insecure
            fallthrough in-addr.arpa ip6.arpa
        }
        prometheus :9153
        forward . /etc/resolv.conf
        cache 30
        loop
        reload
        loadbalance
    }
    dest-cluster.example.com:53 {
        forward . <destination-cluster-dns-ip>
    }
EOF

oc apply -f /tmp/cluster-dns-config.yaml
Subtask 1.3: Set Up Storage Classes and Persistent Volumes
Step 1: Verify Storage Classes on Both Clusters

# Check source cluster storage classes
oc login --token=$SOURCE_CLUSTER_TOKEN --server=$SOURCE_CLUSTER_URL
oc get storageclass

# Check destination cluster storage classes
oc login --token=$DEST_CLUSTER_TOKEN --server=$DEST_CLUSTER_URL
