Best Practices for VM Migration
Planning Phase
• Inventory Assessment: Document all VMs, their dependencies, and resource requirements • Network Planning: Ensure network connectivity and DNS resolution between clusters • Storage Compatibility: Verify storage classes and volume types are compatible • Downtime Planning: Schedule migrations during maintenance windows

Migration Execution
• Backup First: Always create backups before migration • Test Migrations: Perform test migrations with non-critical VMs first • Monitor Resources: Watch cluster resources during migration • Validate Incrementally: Test each component after migration

Post-Migration
• Performance Monitoring: Monitor VM performance for several days • Application Testing: Thoroughly test all applications • Documentation: Update documentation with new cluster information • Cleanup: Remove VMs from source cluster only after validation

